Subject: [PATCH] Metal: offline metallib compile and binary-archive code objects

The published metal_code_object path only covers MSL source JIT. Every
measurement run that sets ACPP_METAL_ENABLE_OFFLINE_METALLIB and
ACPP_METAL_ENABLE_BINARY_ARCHIVE depends on the measured tree's offline path:
spawn metal+metallib under the JIT guard, write durable cache entries, optional
MTL::BinaryArchive transaction save/load, and feature-flag gating.

Extend metal_code_object.hpp/cpp and the kernel_cache offline flag plumbing,
and add the offline-compile unit test, to match the measured tree.

Note: the offline paths are inert unless the runtime env vars are set (see
INSTALL recommendation). Source reproduction only: not compile-verified here.

